FINDINGS / OBSERVATIONS (no criterion failed):
  - Global-per-manager revision means a save to a DIFFERENT scenario between
    preview and apply produces a false-positive 409. This is the accepted
    D-Z-h tradeoff and is documented at settings.go:125-132 (the field),
    494-499 (LoadContextWithRevision) and 816-822 (SaveWithRevisionIfScenario).
    No test pins this behavior; not required by the task.
  - settings.go:679 migration-on-load write does not bump (see C2). Documented
    at 866-869, pre-existing on master, and provably harmless because it runs
    under the load's own held lock. Backlog note only.
  - `expectedScenario == ""` still skips BOTH guards (settings.go:827). No
    production caller uses that path (`grep -rn SaveWithRevisionIfScenario`
    shows handlers.go:244 as the only non-test caller), so it cannot be reached
    with an empty expectation today.
